# Directives and the contexts in which they are applied

## INDEX FILES

If a request URI ends in '/', if an index directive appears in the matched request location,  
the entries in 'index' should be appended to the 'root' directory specified for that location,
and if the file exists and is accessible, should be returned.

If no matching index file is found, and autoindex is set, the program should generate a directory listing for  
the matching request location.

### autoindex

Directives

    Syntax: autoindex on | off;
    Default: autoindex off;
    Context: http, server, location

The autoindex directive indicates whether or not requests ending with the slash character (‘/’) should produce a directory listing.  
Usually a request is passed to an 'autoindex location' when no index file is found.

Example

    location / {
        autoindex on;
    }

### index

Directives

    Syntax:     index file ...;
    Default:    index index.html;
    Context:    global, server, location 

Defines files that will be used as an index. Files are checked in the specified order.  
The last element of the list can be a file with an absolute path. Example:  

Example

    location / {
        index index.html;
    }

